1
00:00:04,964 --> 00:00:06,089
Monica.

2
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:07,842
Hey, can I borrow the Porsche?

3
00:00:07,883 --> 00:00:08,926
Okay.

4
00:00:08,968 --> 00:00:10,010
All right!

5
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:11,219
But, uh...

6
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:12,888
what is it not?

7
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:16,517
A place to entertain
my lady friends.

8
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:18,811
And what else is it not?

9
00:00:18,853 --> 00:00:21,605
A place to eat spaghetti.

10
00:00:21,647 --> 00:00:22,606
Very good.
Thanks.

11
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:24,358
What do you need it for anyway?

12
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:27,026
Oh, the Powerball Lottery
is up to $300 million

13
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,946
and they don't sell tickets
here in New York, so...

14
00:00:28,988 --> 00:00:30,823
Oh, so you're driving
up to Connecticut?

15
00:00:30,865 --> 00:00:35,076
Yeah, Connecticut,
not... West Virginia.

16
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:38,121
Hey, maybe I'll
drive you up there.

17
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:39,874
I'd like to buy
some tickets myself.

18
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:40,875
Yeah, with Chandler

19
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:42,167
not getting paid,

20
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:44,712
we could really use
$300 million.

21
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,881
Yes, because if I was
at my old job,

22
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:49,633
we'd say, "$300 million?
No, thank you."

23
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:52,678
Hey, will you get me
tickets, too?

24
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:53,637
Yeah, me, too.

25
00:00:53,679 --> 00:00:54,638
Sure.

26
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:55,931
Ooh! I have an idea.

27
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:57,307
Why don't we all
pitch in 50 bucks,

28
00:00:57,349 --> 00:00:58,767
we'll pool our money together,

29
00:00:58,809 --> 00:01:00,394
and then if we win,
we'll split it.

30
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:01,436
( all agreeing )

31
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,730
That's a great idea.

32
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:04,481
No, thanks.

33
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:07,693
You don't want
to win the lottery?

34
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:09,028
Uh, sure I do.

35
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,196
I also want to be king
of my own country

36
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:13,741
and find out what happened
to Amelia Earhart.

37
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:15,701
Still on
Amelia Earhart?

38
00:01:15,743 --> 00:01:17,494
The woman just vanished.

39
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:20,956
Seriously, Ross,
you don't want in on this?

40
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:24,083
No. Do you know what your odds
are of winning the lottery?

41
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,794
I mean, you have a better chance

42
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:27,838
of being struck
by lightning 42 times.

43
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,088
Yes, but there's
six of us,

44
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,257
so we'd only have
to get struck

45
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:31,341
by lightning
seven times.

46
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:33,677
I like those odds.

47
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:36,095
Seriously, you guys,
I can't believe

48
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:38,974
you're going to spend
$250 on the lottery.

49
00:01:39,016 --> 00:01:41,810
I mean, that's such
a bunch of boohockey.

50
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:47,024
I'll ask.

51
00:01:47,066 --> 00:01:49,317
Boohockey?

52
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:52,071
Oh, oh, we think Emma's
about to start talking

53
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,822
so we're trying to be careful

54
00:01:53,864 --> 00:01:56,241
about what words
we use in front of her.

55
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:59,661
Yeah, so get ready to hear a lot
of "boohockey," "gosh darn it"

56
00:01:59,703 --> 00:02:01,413
and "brother pucker."

57
00:02:02,998 --> 00:02:04,959
How do you know she's
going to start talking?

58
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,668
Well, when I talk to her,
I almost feel

59
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,336
like she understands
what I'm saying.

60
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:10,338
Kinda like Joey.

61
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,508
What's that now?

62
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:25,938
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

63
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:27,064
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

64
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:30,818
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

65
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:34,780
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

66
00:02:34,822 --> 00:02:37,783
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

67
00:02:37,825 --> 00:02:40,410
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

68
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:44,081
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

69
00:02:44,123 --> 00:02:46,625
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

70
00:02:46,667 --> 00:02:49,086
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

71
00:02:49,128 --> 00:02:51,630
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

72
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:54,758
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

73
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,972
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

74
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:09,106
God, look at all
these tickets.

75
00:03:09,148 --> 00:03:10,440
It's so exciting.

76
00:03:10,482 --> 00:03:12,609
I haven't won anything
since the sixth grade.

77
00:03:12,651 --> 00:03:14,402
Pie-eating contest?

78
00:03:16,864 --> 00:03:18,406
Oh, you assume
because I was heavy

79
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:20,450
that's the only way
I could win something?

80
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:22,911
No, I saw a picture of you
covered in blueberries.

81
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:24,913
That was a good day.

82
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:27,958
They're towing your car!

83
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,208
They're towing
your car!

84
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,210
I parked in a garage on Morton.

85
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:34,422
They're towing a car

86
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:36,215
and I am...

87
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,552
seeing spots.

88
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,554
Oh, my God, Ross,
you don't have Emma.

89
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,014
And Rachel, you
don't have Emma.

90
00:03:42,056 --> 00:03:43,557
Where is Emma?
Who has Emma?!

91
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:46,309
Joey, relax. My mother
picked her up two hours ago.

92
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:47,602
You were there.

93
00:03:48,896 --> 00:03:50,064
I was?

94
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:52,232
Yes, and you talked to her.

95
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:53,483
I did?

96
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:55,777
She dropped off a casserole.

97
00:03:55,819 --> 00:03:58,113
Oh, yeah, the
casserole lady.

98
00:03:58,155 --> 00:03:59,781
So, did you come by

99
00:03:59,823 --> 00:04:01,575
to watch us win
the big bucks?

100
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:03,785
Yeah, and then
I figured, after you win,

101
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:06,997
we can all go out to the balcony
and see a night rainbow

102
00:04:07,039 --> 00:04:08,999
with gremlins dancing
on top of it.

103
00:04:09,041 --> 00:04:10,125
( telephone ringing )

104
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,376
Don't touch the phone!

105
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:13,420
I'll get it,
I'll get it,
I'll get it!

106
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,671
Hello.

107
00:04:14,713 --> 00:04:16,464
You think he washed
his hands?

108
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,758
Hey, Charlie, what do you know?

109
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:19,009
What's going on?

110
00:04:19,051 --> 00:04:20,510
Chandler's supposed to find out

111
00:04:20,552 --> 00:04:22,763
if he's getting an assistant job
at his ad agency

112
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:25,057
but out of 15 interns,
they're only hiring three.

113
00:04:25,099 --> 00:04:27,059
Ooh, tough odds.

114
00:04:27,101 --> 00:04:29,186
Yeah, if only
it were a sure thing

115
00:04:29,228 --> 00:04:30,979
like your 24-state lottery.

116
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:34,482
Yeah, look who's coming around.

117
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:38,737
Damn it. All right,
call me when you know more.

118
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,823
JOEY:
Did you get it?

119
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:43,992
One of the slots got filled.

120
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:46,203
By you?

121
00:04:46,245 --> 00:04:48,872
Sense the tone.

122
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:52,417
No, that kid Nate got it.

123
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:53,752
Oh, I hate that guy.

124
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:55,879
Come on, kid,
pull up your pants!

125
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:57,296
I know.

126
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:59,216
Well, there's
two spots left, right?

127
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:01,135
Yeah. I mean,
I want this so much.

128
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:02,594
I mean,
I want to get one,

129
00:05:02,636 --> 00:05:04,721
