home from work.

138
00:05:22,281 --> 00:05:25,159
A psychic and a wishbone?

139
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,912
Guys, give someone
else a chance.

140
00:05:28,954 --> 00:05:30,497
All right, who
wants to do it?

141
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:31,957
Oh, can I?

142
00:05:31,999 --> 00:05:34,375
Vegetarians never get
to do the wishbone.

143
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:36,003
It's really not fair either,

144
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:37,879
because, you know, just
because we don't eat the meat

145
00:05:37,921 --> 00:05:40,215
doesn't mean we don't like
to play with the carcasses.

146
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,218
All right. Hey, Rach?

147
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,552
No, I'm good--
I don't want to get

148
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:45,846
that turkey smell
all over my hands.

149
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,222
I'll do it!

150
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:49,599
Got to get the casserole stink
off of mine.

151
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:51,852
Okay.

152
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,145
I hope I win.

153
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:54,688
Well, it doesn't really matter.

154
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,773
You're both wishing
for the same thing, right?

155
00:05:56,815 --> 00:06:00,443
I can't tell you what I'm
wishing for, or else, you know,

156
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:01,736
it won't come true.

157
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:05,032
Right, but we know
what you're wishing for.

158
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:06,700
I can't really say.

159
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,327
I understand,
but you're wishing

160
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:10,912
for what we think you're
wishing for, aren't you?

161
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,123
I'm not really comfortable
with these questions.

162
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:16,084
Please!
Just do it.

163
00:06:16,126 --> 00:06:17,376
Okay, ready: one, two...

164
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:18,461
three!

165
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:19,587
I won. Hey!

166
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:20,797
You know what?

167
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:22,883
I'm sure your wish
is gonna come true,

168
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:26,261
but, you guys, just in case,
maybe a genie will come out

169
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,888
if we rub this lamp... Ow!

170
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,350
That thing gets hot!

171
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:33,518
You know, Ross, just
keep making your jokes.

172
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,936
How are you
going to feel

173
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:36,271
if we actually do win?

174
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:37,856
Uh, you're not gonna win.

175
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:39,941
Oh, I know, I know,
the odds are against us,

176
00:06:39,983 --> 00:06:41,985
but somebody has to win,
and it could be us

177
00:06:42,027 --> 00:06:43,570
and then how you gonna feel?

178
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:45,697
You know, we're gonna be all
like, "Oh, everybody

179
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:47,782
let's take our helicopters
up to the Cape,"

180
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,993
and you're gonna,
and you're gonna be all like,

181
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:52,371
"Oh, I can't, guys,
I'll have to meet you up there.

182
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,830
I gotta gas up the Hyundai."

183
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:01,046
Okay, I've heard myself on tape
and I sound nothing like that.

184
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,132
I can see the headline now.

185
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:06,676
"Lottery Winners' Friend,
Filled With Regret,

186
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:07,928
Eats Own Arm."

187
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:10,097
Why would I
eat my own arm?

188
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,348
You wouldn't,
but we own the paper.

189
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,473
We can print whatever we want.

190
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:14,642
You know what, Ross?

191
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:16,644
I'm going to throw in
50 bucks for you.

192
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:17,645
Why?

193
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:18,646
Because I know

194
00:07:18,688 --> 00:07:19,731
that you think

195
00:07:19,773 --> 00:07:21,316
that the lottery
is boohockey...

196
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,153
but we're all here
and we're gonna

197
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:26,738
watch the numbers
and have fun.

198
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,073
And you're my brother

199
00:07:28,115 --> 00:07:29,824
and I want you to
be a part of this.

200
00:07:31,201 --> 00:07:32,994
You don't have to do that.

201
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:34,996
I mean, I'll pay for myself,

202
00:07:35,038 --> 00:07:36,539
but just the fact that

203
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,499
you want me to have
fun with you guys,

204
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,876
that's so sweet.
Come here.

205
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:43,422
Get a room.

206
00:07:47,342 --> 00:07:48,760
Okay, so, now that you're in,

207
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:50,387
what are you gonna do if we win?

208
00:07:50,429 --> 00:07:52,347
I don't know.
I'll probably just invest it.

209
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:53,807
Ooh, calm down.

210
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:56,684
Seriously,
that's your fantasy?

211
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:58,186
To invest it?

212
00:07:58,228 --> 00:07:59,896
Oh, I'm sorry.
Did I say invest it?

213
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:01,815
I meant
be cool and piss it all away.

214
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:05,444
Ooh! Ooh! I know.

215
00:08:05,484 --> 00:08:07,528
We should pool
all our money

216
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,030
and buy the Knicks.

217
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:11,199
I don't really care
about the Knicks.

218
00:08:11,241 --> 00:08:14,369
Oh, you will when I pick you
as starting forward.

219
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:16,830
You would do that?

220
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:18,790
I never get picked.

221
00:08:18,832 --> 00:08:21,001
You know, I'm not
sure a sports team
is the way to go.

222
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:22,752
You're not going
to let me buy the Knicks?

223
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,796
I can't believe you're taking
this away from me.

224
00:08:24,838 --> 00:08:28,216
You're right, it has been
your dream for over 15 seconds.

225
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:32,511
Uh, how long until they
announce the numbers, Mommy?

226
00:08:33,512 --> 00:08:35,556
I'll take this one, too.

227
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:38,059
Uh... "Mommy"?

228
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:40,354
Oh, I've gotten into the habit

229
00:08:40,395 --> 00:08:43,982
of calling Rachel "Mommy"
when we're around Emma,

230
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:46,485
which, I now realize,
we are not.

231
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:50,571
I'm hoping that if
she hears it enough,

232
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:51,948
it'll be her
first word.

233
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,533
Although, if we're
going to do that,

234
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:55,202
we should probably
call me Daddy, too.

235
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:58,372
Ooh. I like that, Daddy.

236
00:09:02,501 --> 00:09:05,920
I, uh... I was just
talking about Rachel.

237
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:08,298
Ooh, is Daddy getting angry?

238
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:13,594
Is Daddy going to spank me?

239
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,931
Well, that depends.

240
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:19,267
Have you been a bad g...

241
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:20,643
No, I can't. I can't.

242
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,105
( telephone ringing )

243
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:25,440
Hello. Hello.

244
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:28,818
Hey, Charlie, did
anybody else hear?

245
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,695
What? Susan got it?

246
00:09:30,737 --> 00:09:32,030
How?

247
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:34,366
Oh, man, I would
have slept with him.

248
00:09:34,408 --> 00:09:36,284
All right. Bye.

249
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:39,204
Dude, I'm sorry,

250
00:09:39,246 --> 00:09:41,248
but, hey, there's
one spot left, right?

251
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,916
Well, Charlie's
gonna get that.

252
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:44,125
Hey, don't say that.

253
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:45,460
You got just as
good a chance

254
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:46,878
as anybody else of
getting that job.

255
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,755
He is the boss's son.

256
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:50,589
Come on, lottery!

257
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:52,384
Yeah! Yeah!
Oop! Ooh, you guys,

258
00:09:52,426 --> 00:09:53,927
it starts in, like,
20 minutes.

259
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,178
Okay, all right,
here we go.

260
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,930
So, we need to sort
through the tickets

261
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,848
as quickly as possible
to see if we've won.

262
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:01,226
So does anybody have
any ideas how to organize this?

263
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:02,269
Okay, how about this?

264
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:05,897
We divide them
into six groups of 40

265
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:07,607
and the remaining ten
can be read

266
00:10:07,648 --> 00:10:09,526
by whoever finishes
their pile first.

267
00:10:09,568 --> 00:10:10,651
Oh, I have another idea.

268
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:12,487
I'm sorry-- idea time is over.

269
00:10:12,529 --> 00:10:14,322
Okay, well,

270
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:15,865
are all the tickets
in the bowl?

271
00:10:15,907 --> 00:10:17,284
Yeah.

272
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:18,785
What about the ones
you have on the nightstand?

273
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:20,703
There are no tickets
on the nightstand.

274
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,414
Yes, there are.
I just saw them

275
00:10:22,456 --> 00:10:24,249
a few minutes ago.

276
00:10:24,291 --> 00:10:25,417
Uh, no, you didn't.

277
00:10:25,459 --> 00:10:26,751
You must be mistaken.

278
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:27,877
Honey, there are

279
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:29,296
like 20 tickets
on the nightstand.

280
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:31,256
Chandler, sense the tone.

281
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,134
Well, well, well.

282
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:36,094
Look what Mommy found.

283
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,431
Okay, fine.

284
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:41,433
I bought 20 extra tickets
for me and Chandler.

285
00:10:41,475 --> 00:10:43,017
( gasps )

286
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:45,395
The psychic also said
that I would be betrayed.

287
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:48,273
I can't believe this.

288
00:10:48,315 --> 00:10:49,941
I thought we were all
in this together.

289
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:52,026
Hey, you just got in
five minutes ago.

290
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,487
Three minutes ago.

291
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:56,197
I don't know
why that's important.

292
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:57,491
Oh, look, hey,
I was with you

293
00:10:57,532 --> 00:10:59,200
the whole time we
were in Connecticut.

294
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:00,660
When did you
even get those?

295
00:11:00,701 --> 00:11:02,496
When you were reading
the dirty magazines

296
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:04,038
without taking off the plastic.

297
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,082
I'll show you how.

298
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:10,420
Okay, well, Monica, suppose one
of your special tickets wins.

299
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:13,006
How are you going to feel
when you win the lottery

300
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:14,799
and you lose all your friends?

301
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:17,885
Please, if I win the lottery,
you guys are not gonna leave me.

302
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:20,514
Someone gave me a basket
of mini-muffins last week

303
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:22,890
and I couldn't get rid
of you for three days.

304
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:25,435
Chandler, would
you just tell her

305
00:11:25,477 --> 00:11:27,228
what she did
was wrong?

306
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:29,397
She's right. You shouldn't
have bought tickets

307
00:11:29,439 --> 00:11:30,398
just for us.

308
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,193
Let me finish.
However...

309
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:35,069
it doesn't look like
I'm gonna get this job

310
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:36,695
so I can't afford
to have principles.

311
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:38,239
So screw you!
The tickets are ours!

312
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:39,907
( gasps )

313
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:41,618
There's the man I married.

314
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,913
All right. Believe me,
if you win the lottery

315
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,748
it's the last you're
gonna hear from us.

316
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,584
Fine. Don't be my friends.

317
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:52,045
I'll buy new friends.

318
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:54,922
Yeah, and then I'll pay
for their plastic surgery

319
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,633
so they'd look
just like you.

320
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:58,759
All right, you know what?
That's it.

321
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:00,595
I want my share
of the tickets.

322
00:12:00,637 --> 00:12:01,929
Yeah, I want
my tickets, too--

323
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:03,181
and I'm buying the Knicks...

324
00:12:03,223 --> 00:12:04,723
and Steffi Graf!

325
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:05,850
( chortles )

326
00:12:05,892 --> 00:12:07,435
Hold it-- then I want

327
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:09,187
mine, too, and if I win,

328
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:11,814
I'm going to put it all
into a very low-yield bond.

329
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,525
No! You guys,
we got to keep

330
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:15,151
all the tickets together.

331
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:17,278
MONICA:
No, no!

332
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,489
We should divide them up,
and I should get extra

333
00:12:19,531 --> 00:12:21,199
because we used
my car to buy them!

334
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:24,118
Hey! Hey! If anybody gets
extra tickets, it should be me!

335
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,704
This whole thing
was my idea!

336
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:28,831
Oh, yeah, thanks
for inventing the lottery.

337
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:30,291
RACHEL:
That's it.

338
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,377
Just give them to me
and I'll split them up.

339
00:12:32,419 --> 00:12:34,212
Ow!
( shrieks )

340
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:35,213
Hey, hey.

341
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:37,257
( shrieks )

342
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:38,757
I can't take it anymore!

343
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:40,468
I'm putting an end to this!

344
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:42,095
Okay, if she jumps,
I get her tickets.

345
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:43,137
Wait! No, no!
Hey, hey!

346
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:46,725
If we're not
doing this together,

347
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:48,268
we're not doing it at all.

348
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:49,894
Say good-bye
to your tickets.

349
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:51,354
No! No! No!

350
00:12:51,396 --> 00:12:53,356
Do not come any closer!

351
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:55,483
Can I come a
little bit closer?

352
00:12:55,525 --> 00:12:58,027
Valuable things are
getting squished.

353
00:12:58,069 --> 00:12:59,571
Now, what's more important?

354
00:12:59,613 --> 00:13:00,905
Your friends, or money?

355
00:13:00,947 --> 00:13:02,949
Friends!
Friends!
Money!

356
00:13:06,536 --> 00:13:08,413
Friends.

357
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:11,666
And, Monica, what about
your extra tickets?

358
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,376
They're all in there.

359
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:16,379
Even these five
that I hid in my bra.

360
00:13:16,421 --> 00:13:17,714
Monica!

361
00:13:17,756 --> 00:13:19,382
Okay. Good.

362
00:13:19,424 --> 00:13:20,841
You guys were so scared.

363
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:23,010
There was no way I was
gonna dump this thing...

364
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:24,178
( shrieks )

365
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,555
God! No!

366
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,603
I think I broke your bowl.

367
00:13:31,645 --> 00:13:33,772
Go! Go! Go!

368
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:35,106
Go! Go!

369
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:50,246
What a beautiful night

370
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:52,957
to be running around the street
looking for tickets.

371
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:55,960
And the wind sure made it fun.

372
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:58,463
Phoebe, we lost
half of them.

373
00:13:58,505 --> 00:14:01,466
So what? Monica,
we have the winning ticket.

374
00:14:01,508 --> 00:14:03,968
My psychic said I was going
to win, remember?

375
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:09,098
Weird your psychic
didn't mention anything
about the scary pigeon.

376
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:14,187
As a matter of fact, she said
that's how I'm going to die.

377
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:17,565
So excuse me for being
a little skittish.

378
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:20,318
Hey, there's two messages.

379
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,361
This could be from work.

380
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:22,779
Play them.
Okay.

381
00:14:22,821 --> 00:14:24,447
Here we go.

382
00:14:24,489 --> 00:14:26,157
( beep )

383
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:29,160
PHOEBE:
Hello? This is the pigeon
from the balcony

384
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:31,788
calling to apologize.

385
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:34,415
I shouldn't have
knocked the tickets

386
00:14:34,457 --> 00:14:38,169
out of the pretty lady's hand.

387
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:40,547
It was all my fault--
not hers.

388
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,549
Bye. Coo.

389
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:51,891
Well, I bet that was
very hard for him to do.

390
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:53,685
( beep )

391
00:14:53,727 --> 00:14:55,936
Hey, Chandler, it's Charlie.

392
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,438
This is it. Shh!

393
00:14:57,480 --> 00:15:01,860
Listen, um, it turns out
I got the last spot.

394
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,236
I'm really sorry, man.

395
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:05,029
It was a lot of fun
working with you.

396
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:06,906
Give me a call if you want.

397
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:11,828
Gosh, I'm so sorry, honey.

398
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:12,871
Sorry about that, man.

399
00:15:12,911 --> 00:15:14,539
That is so unfair.

400
00:15:14,581 --> 00:15:17,375
It's like that time they
promoted Sandra over me at work.

401
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:19,335
Oh, was she related
to Ralph Lauren?

402
00:15:19,377 --> 00:15:23,798
No, she was just much better
at her job than me.

403
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,717
Guys, the drawing's
about to start.

404
00:15:25,759 --> 00:15:27,301
We should call my mom's house

405
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:29,303
and say good night to Emma
before she goes down.

406
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:30,638
Oh, yeah, it's a good idea.

407
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,933
Honey, you're being
very strong about this.

408
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:36,644
I know how badly
you wanted that job.

409
00:15:36,686 --> 00:15:39,856
Yeah, you know, I really
thought I deserved it.

410
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:41,566
But let's go win
the lottery.

411
00:15:41,608 --> 00:15:44,193
I mean, we still have
130 chances to win, right?

412
00:15:46,153 --> 00:15:47,697
131.

413
00:15:50,617 --> 00:15:52,702
Good night, sweetheart.
I love you.

414
00:15:52,744 --> 00:15:56,873
And remember, you're
Daddy's little girl.

415
00:15:56,915 --> 00:15:59,751
Phoebe's totally
ruined that for me.

416
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:05,465
Hi, Mom.
Oh, put her back on.
( TV plays )

417
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:08,050
Rach, come on, they're
announcing the numbers.

418
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:09,968
My God, I can already
feel myself changing.

419
00:16:12,138 --> 00:16:13,807
Here are your official
Powerball numbers.

420
00:16:13,848 --> 00:16:15,558
We have 53.

421
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,643
I've got that.

422
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:18,227
Ooh, ooh, ooh,
we have one, too.

423
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:20,480
We are on the road, people.

424
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,356
Check those tickets carefully.

425
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,733
Come on!

426
00:16:23,775 --> 00:16:26,193
Mom, please.
I know you love your new lips.

427
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:29,238
But I can barely understand you.

428
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:32,575
Would you please just let me
say good night to my daughter?

429
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:35,119
...and here we go,
the Powerball is seven.

430
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:36,871
All right, check your numbers!

431
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:39,039
Make me rich.

432
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:40,750
Have a safe, happy holiday.
Good night.

433
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:42,502
Oh, guys, you're not going
to believe this.

434
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:44,044
I was just saying
good night to Emma

435
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:46,046
and she said
her first words.

436
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,256
What?
Really?

437
00:16:47,298 --> 00:16:48,341
What did she say?

438
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:50,885
She said "gleba."

439
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:57,433
Make me rich!

440
00:16:57,475 --> 00:16:59,268
Isn't that amazing?

441
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:01,228
Yeah, no, no, no.
That's great.

442
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,356
Why aren't you
more excited?

443
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:07,025
Uh, Rach, "gleba" is not a word.

444
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:10,070
Well, of course it is.

445
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:12,239
Okay, what does it mean?

446
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:15,451
Well, I don't know
all the words.

447
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:18,621
You know, I'm just glad I didn't
miss my daughter's first word.

448
00:17:18,663 --> 00:17:20,456
Well, yes, you did.

449
00:17:20,498 --> 00:17:22,124
"Gleba" is a word.

450
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:23,877
Okay, use it in a sentence.

451
00:17:23,918 --> 00:17:26,671
Okay.
Uh, "Emma just said gleba."

452
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:32,343
It's not a word.

453
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:34,012
Okay, okay, okay, fine.

454
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,095
I'm going to look it up.

455
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,639
Oh, oh, okay, great.

456
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:38,265
You know what,
while you're at it,

457
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:39,893
she said another word
the other day.

458
00:17:39,934 --> 00:17:42,144
Why don't you look up...
( sputters )

459
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,735
All right, okay, okay, gleba.

460
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:51,654
Gleba, gleba... gleba!
Ah, here it is.

461
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:55,825
"The fleshy, spore-bearing
inner mass of a certain fungi."

462
00:18:01,039 --> 00:18:05,167
She's going to be
a scientist.

463
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:13,051
Damn it.

464
00:18:13,091 --> 00:18:14,594
Anybody got
anything?
No.

465
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:16,888
I'm still
looking through mine.

466
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:18,598
Just double checking.

467
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:22,685
No. No. No.

468
00:18:28,066 --> 00:18:29,233
No!

469
00:18:29,275 --> 00:18:31,778
( telephone rings )

470
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:34,447
Hello?

471
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:36,032
Hold on.

472
00:18:36,074 --> 00:18:37,533
It's your boss.

473
00:18:37,575 --> 00:18:40,244
Ah, the I'm-sorry-
I-rejected-you phone call.

474
00:18:40,286 --> 00:18:42,288
Not used to getting
these from guys.

475
00:18:44,082 --> 00:18:45,207
Hey, Steve.

476
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,043
Chandler, hi.

477
00:18:47,085 --> 00:18:49,796
I'm sure you've heard
we filled the three positions.

478
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:52,339
We just felt that with
your maturity and experience,

479
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:55,009
you wouldn't be happy
being someone's assistant.

480
00:18:55,051 --> 00:18:57,136
Well, no, no, I'd love to be
somebody's assistant.

481
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:59,806
Answering phones, getting
coffee, I live for that stuff.

482
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,641
And I'm not too mature.

483
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,977
Farts, boobies, butt cracks.

484
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:10,066
Chandler, you were the strongest
person in the program.

485
00:19:10,108 --> 00:19:13,820
We're offering you the position
of junior copywriter.

486
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:18,365
Me? The guy who just said
"butt cracks"?

487
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:19,951
Yes, that's right.

488
00:19:19,993 --> 00:19:21,744
We're excited about
the level of sophistication

489
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:23,830
you'll be bringing to the job.

490
00:19:25,915 --> 00:19:27,875
Okay, well, thanks.
You won't regret it.

491
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:29,794
I'll see you tomorrow.

492
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:43,766
What?

493
00:19:43,808 --> 00:19:46,853
Oh, yeah, I'm going to
be a junior copywriter.

494
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:49,187
Wow!
That's great!
Congratulations.

495
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:51,357
Sweetie,
I'm so proud of you.

496
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,901
Does that mean I get
the good loving tonight?

497
00:19:53,943 --> 00:19:55,111
You bet.

498
00:19:55,153 --> 00:19:58,364
No TV or anything.

499
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:00,574
Hey, that is so great
about the job.

500
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:02,326
Thanks, man.

501
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,244
And I'd like to
think I had a little
something to do with it.

502
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:05,496
Really, why?

503
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:07,707
Well, before,
with the wishbone...

504
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:10,751
I, uh... I didn't wish
we would win the lottery.

505
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,753
I wished you'd
get the job.

506
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:15,631
Oh, yeah?

507
00:20:15,673 --> 00:20:18,425
Listen, don't tell Monica.
She'll rip your heart right out.

508
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:20,260
Oh, yeah.

509
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:23,681
Wow, you know what?

510
00:20:23,723 --> 00:20:25,265
There was a little part of me

511
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:27,267
that really thought
we were going to win.

512
00:20:27,309 --> 00:20:29,103
Me, too.

513
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:33,941
So much for my
dinosaur-slash-Amelia Earhart
theme park.

514
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:36,276
You guys...

515
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,404
what was the Powerball
number again?

516
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:40,198
Seven.

517
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:41,323
We won.

518
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:42,366
What?

519
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:43,409
We won!
What?!
Let me see!

520
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:44,493
Let me see!

521
00:20:44,535 --> 00:20:46,286
Don't tear it.

522
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:49,623
Phoebe, you don't have
any of the first five numbers.

523
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:52,626
I know that.

524
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:54,712
But look, we got
the Powerball number.

525
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:56,630
We won three dollars!

526
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:00,551
Wow, you think we should
get that over 20 years

527
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:02,386
or go for the big payout?

528
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:05,723
I don't care, I've never
won anything before.

529
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:07,600
I can't believe this!

530
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:10,019
So, Pheebs, what are
you going to do with
your three dollars?

531
00:21:10,061 --> 00:21:11,896
Well, it's not all mine.

532
00:21:11,938 --> 00:21:13,397
We all get 50 cents.

533
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:16,650
You know what,
you can have mine.

534
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:17,860
Me, too.

535
00:21:17,902 --> 00:21:18,861
Me, too.

536
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:20,988
Me, too.

537
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:28,579
Well, I guess
if everybody else is.

538
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,173
Hey, guys.

539
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:41,008
I just called the
Powerball hotline.

540
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:43,136
Can you believe it?
Nobody won.

541
00:21:43,177 --> 00:21:46,973
I beg to differ.

542
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:49,934
Maybe nobody
won the jackpot,

543
00:21:49,976 --> 00:21:51,852
but there was this guy
in here earlier

544
00:21:51,894 --> 00:21:54,063
and he found a ticket
on the street, right outside,

545
00:21:54,105 --> 00:21:56,690
and won $10,000.

546
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,286
Coo. Again...

547
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:11,497
don't blame the pretty lady.

548
00:22:11,538 --> 00:22:13,249
It was not her fault.

549
00:22:13,291 --> 00:22:16,669
It was me, the pigeon. Coo.

550
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:22,716
Seriously,
stop staring at her.

551
00:22:28,973 --> 00:22:31,892
